From 480917b8b42c782bb0cdde5f441a18d1b754a66a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xenia UI <ui@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] [App] Add SettingsModel: typed access to every config
 option

UI-independent layer over the cvar registry:

* Enumerate() lists every persistent option with its category, description and
  type; values are read/written through a typed variant.
* Saved vs in-use values are distinguished, so a UI can tell when a command
  line argument or a per-game config overrides what is saved.
* GameOverrides edits <config>/config/<TITLEID>.config.toml, storing only the
  options changed for that game, using the same nested-category layout the
  loader expects. Unrelated keys already in the file are kept, and a file that
  fails to parse is never overwritten.
